// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), oscd.community, Natalia Shornikova
// Date: 2020-10-14 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1216
// Description: Detects calls to "SyncInvoke" that is part of the "CL_Invocation.ps1" script to proxy execution
//   using "System.Diagnostics.Process"
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Scripts/Cl_invocation/
//   - https://twitter.com/bohops/status/948061991012327424
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_cl_invocation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "SyncInvoke "
